From: tcmay@netcom.com (Timothy C. May)
Subject: Glocks and other fine weaponry

Elias Israel writes:

> Well, now that I'm officially a "gun nut," I'm all for more discussions
> of such things here on the list, though I suppose that some people
> would rather hear about bath tubs. How close to a "core value" is gun
> ownership to the list? Somewhere in between bath tubs and nanotech, I
> guess. Is this a discussion that should continue here, or should it
> be "terminated with extreme prejudice?"

The fact that the gun threads have been popular and that many List
members are either shopping for guns, have bought them, are going to
the practice ranges, or are otherwise active should tell us something.

I think there are several reasons why this thread has an Extropian
connection:

1. Survival. Guns are about protecting oneself rather than relying on
the State to do it for you. 

2. Gun bans press a lot of buttons for Libertarians and Extropians.
The politics of the liberal "victim disarmament" movement and their
socialist utopian ideas are anathema to many of us. Hence, guns
provide a practical touchstone for debate about our ideas.

3. Technology. The technology is fun to talk about, for many folks.
Others may find it less fun, in which case they can ignore it.

4. Timeliness. The "time value" of the current discussion of guns has
gone way up, as the rush to ban guns continues. The gun control
advocates like Sarah Brady and Dianne Feinstein are literally freaking
out as the rush to buy guns and stock up on "evil" bullets
accelerates. Across the country, gun stores are reporting record
sales, to women especially. That several List members have bought guns
very recently shows the timeliness of this discussion.

Thus, I think it's a perfectly fine topic for the List.

--Tim May


