From: eder@hsvaic.hv.boeing.com (Dani Eder)
Subject: Planet brains without guns

I remind the recent poster who suggested Planet-sized brains
would be good to find ways of living without guns of the
'Kzinti Lesson':

Every reaction engine is also a weapon.

I would generalize this to say that every high energy technology
can also be used as a weapon.  The Kzinti Lesson appeared in
a Larry Niven story about an 'unarmed' human spacecraft encountering
a warlike race of 8 foot cats called the Kzin.  The humans win by
pointing their Gigawatt photon thruster (big laser), which was the
main ship propulsion, at the Kzinti ship, slicing it in two.

The electrostatic fusion reactor that Robert Bussard is developing
couples well to a neutral particle beam generator making (a)
a thuster with an exhaust velocity of 0.2c (good for interstellar
missions), and (b) a heck of a weapon directly up to 1000km
ranges, or by long range
by accelerating  'rocks' to high speed.  At a few percent of c,
a rock packs as much energy per kg as a nuclear bomb.

So, the hope that the future might be weaponless is a forlorn
one as long as high energy technology is there.

Dani Eder

