Some time back, someone had been asking about GPS (Global Positioning
System) mapping options for the Newton.  The current MacWeek reports on the
ETE Communicator, by ETE Inc. of San Diego, CA, a unit that will enable a
host of mobile communications options including cellular phone, fax modem,
GPS navigation, and packet-radio capabilities.  Surprisingly, the unit has
been initially designed for the Sharp ExpertPad, but Newton MP
compatability will surely follow, since Sharp is not quite happy with
ExpertPad sales. The ETE Communicator seems to be essentially a dock onto
which the ExpertPad clips.  It also uses the Jabra Ear-Phone for its human
interface.  The price for the base system (phone/fax) is supposed to be
$500, and additional modules for GPS or packet-radio will be $500.

